The correct fflib method for registering platform events to publish after a successful commit is `registerPublishAfterSuccessfulCommit` taking an `fflib_ISObjectUnitOfWork.IDML`... actually the real signature is `registerPublishAfterSuccessfulCommit(SObject[] records)` — but the error says it doesn't exist with that signature, meaning the deployed fflib version uses `registerPublishAfterSuccessfulCommit(List<SObject>)` is not available; instead it likely only accepts a single `SObject` or uses a different method name entirely. Checking the standard fflib API, the correct method is `registerPublishAfterSuccessfulCommit(List<SObject> records)` on the newer versions, but older versions only have `registerPublishBeforeTransaction` / `registerPublishAfterSuccessfulCommit` taking `SObject` (singular) and iterating. I'll adjust to call it per-record to be safe, and cast to `List<SObject>`.

