The test confirms what I flagged: calling `Messaging.sendEmail` once per opportunity inside the loop hits the 10-invocations-per-transaction limit when 200 opportunities are passed in. I need to fix this while still satisfying "if one email fails the rest still go out" — the correct way to do that in a bulk-safe manner is to batch the calls (e.g., chunks of 10, the max allowed per call) and use `allOrNoneFailures = false` so a bad email in a chunk doesn't stop the others in that chunk, while still only consuming one of the 10 available invocations per chunk.

File: force-app/main/default/classes/RenewalReminderService.cls
```apex
public with sharing class RenewalReminderService {

    // Governor limit: Messaging.sendEmail can be called at most 10 times per transaction.
    private static final Integer MAX_SEND_EMAIL_CALLS = 10;

    /**
     * Sends a renewal reminder email to the owner of each opportunity passed in.
     *
     * Messaging.sendEmail is limited to 10 invocations per transaction, so with
     * up to 200 opportunities per call we cannot call it once per opportunity
     * (that would require up to 200 invocations and throw a LimitException).
     * Instead, emails are batched into chunks of up to 200/10 = 20 messages per
     * call (so the whole batch fits well within the 10-call limit), and each
     * call uses allOrNoneFailures = false so that one bad email within a chunk
     * does not prevent the other emails in that same chunk - or in other
     * chunks - from being sent. The per-message SendEmailResult tells us
     * exactly which messages succeeded.
     *
     * @param opportunityIds up to 200 Opportunity Ids (per the caller's contract)
     * @return the number of emails sent successfully
     */
    public static Integer sendReminders(List<Id> opportunityIds) {
        Integer sentCount = 0;

        if (opportunityIds == null || opportunityIds.isEmpty()) {
            return sentCount;
        }

        List<Opportunity> opportunities = [
            SELECT Id, Name, CloseDate, OwnerId, Owner.IsActive
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE Id IN :opportunityIds
        ];

        List<Messaging.SingleEmailMessage> emails = new List<Messaging.SingleEmailMessage>();

        for (Opportunity opp : opportunities) {
            if (opp.OwnerId == null || opp.Owner.IsActive == false) {
                // No valid user to email; skip rather than let sendEmail throw.
                continue;
            }

            Messaging.SingleEmailMessage email = new Messaging.SingleEmailMessage();
            email.setTargetObjectId(opp.OwnerId);
            email.setSaveAsActivity(false);
            email.setSubject('Renewal due: ' + opp.Name);
            email.setPlainTextBody(
                'This is a reminder that the opportunity "' + opp.Name +
                '" has a renewal due. The close date is ' +
                (opp.CloseDate != null ? opp.CloseDate.format() : 'not set') +
                '. Please review and take any necessary action.'
            );

            emails.add(email);
        }

        if (emails.isEmpty()) {
            return sentCount;
        }

        // Chunk size chosen so that even 200 opportunities need at most
        // ceil(200 / chunkSize) calls, comfortably under the 10-call limit.
        Integer chunkSize = 20;
        Integer startIndex = 0;

        while (startIndex < emails.size()) {
            Integer endIndex = Math.min(startIndex + chunkSize, emails.size());
            List<Messaging.SingleEmailMessage> chunk = new List<Messaging.SingleEmailMessage>();
            for (Integer i = startIndex; i < endIndex; i++) {
                chunk.add(emails[i]);
            }

            try {
                // allOrNoneFailures = false: a failure for one message in the
                // chunk does not stop the others in the same chunk from being sent.
                Messaging.SendEmailResult[] results = Messaging.sendEmail(chunk, false);

                if (results != null) {
                    for (Messaging.SendEmailResult result : results) {
                        if (result.isSuccess()) {
                            sentCount++;
                        } else {
                            System.debug(
                                LoggingLevel.ERROR,
                                'Failed to send renewal reminder: ' + result.getErrors()
                            );
                        }
                    }
                }
            } catch (Exception e) {
                // Should be rare since allOrNoneFailures = false avoids most
                // per-message exceptions, but guard against unexpected errors
                // (e.g. malformed message) so remaining chunks still get sent.
                System.debug(
                    LoggingLevel.ERROR,
                    'Failed to send a batch of renewal reminders: ' + e.getMessage()
                );
            }

            startIndex = endIndex;
        }

        return sentCount;
    }
}
